join detective right
detective: I’ve come to the conclusion that you must have broken the vase.
join gardener left
gardener: What?
detective: Everyone else has a pretty strong alibi. 
detective: By process of elimination, you must have broken the vase. 
gardener (antsy) : …
gardener: ……
gardener (guilty) : …………………
gardener (speaking) : I-I broke the vase. 
gardener: …
gardener: I was upstairs earlier. 
gardener: I-I was looking for valuables.
gardener (antsy) : …to steal.
gardener: …
gardener: I know it’s wrong, but. Well.
gardener: You see, I’ve come on awful hard times.
gardener (speaking) : Ol’ Drac’ had more money than he knew what to do with.
gardener: I might’ve had an idea or two of what to do with it.
gardener: I thought maybe I’d be able to help out my family and…
gardener (antsy) : …get myself a roof to live under?
gardener: A real one? Not just some ol’ shed in a vampire’s back garden?
gardener (guilty) : …
gardener: …Is that too much to ask for?
gardener (speaking) : Well. 
gardener: I wish I could apologize to the ol’ Count, but I s’pose it’s a bit too late for that.
detective: So you were only upstairs to steal Dracula’s belongings?
gardener: …yeah.
gardener: I may be a petty thief, but I’m no killer.
